# problem #15: contiguous buffers of the window in focus come back through a
# cleared window, not by moving the game on the other monitor out. On the
# host (2026-11-10 20:45) Chrome's 130 MB buffers sat in sysmem, 379 MB of WoW
# went out "for the foreground again", and the buffers still did not fit
# ("restore failed 4"): free bytes are no place for a contiguous buffer.
cap 11000
set longest 64
proc 1614 kwin_wayland old
proc 2617 chrome old chunk=16
proc 12557 game old chunk=64

act 1614 0 4
mark the browser alone, focused: three contiguous buffers and ordinary memory
hint 2617 f
act 2617 0 20
target 2617 600 0.8
alloc 2617 390 n=3 contig   # 3 x 130 MB
at 6

mark the game takes the focus and nearly all of vidmem: the browser, hidden, pays
hint 2617 h
hint 12557 f
act 12557 0 30
act 2617 30 0
target 12557 10850 0.75 spread=20
at 40
expect evicted 2617 >= 860

mark back to the browser, the game stays visible on the other monitor and keeps drawing
hint 12557 v
hint 2617 f
act 2617 0 20
step
at 60
expect evicted 2617 == 0         # everything back, the contiguous buffers too
expect windows 2617 >= 3         # each through a window cleared for it
expect restorefails 2617 <= 3    # no retry storm
expect moved_out 12557 <= 1600   # the game gives what the browser's ordinary memory needs, not 3 x 130 MB more
